/* book Worked example: Q: A short dipole (D = 1.5) receives a 100 MHz wave of power density S = 10 µW/m², polarization matched. Find its maximum effective aperture and the power delivered to a conjugate-matched load, in watts and dBm.
   1. λ = c/f = 3 m.
   2. Aem = Dλ²/4π = 1.5 × 9/12.566 = 1.074 m².
   3. Pr = S Aem = 10 × 10⁻⁶ × 1.074 = 1.074 × 10⁻⁵ W = 10.7 µW.
   4. In dBm: 10 log₁₀(1.074 × 10⁻⁵ / 10⁻³) = 10 log₁₀(0.01074) = −19.7 dBm.
   Answer: Aem = 1.07 m²; Pr = 10.7 µW = −19.7 dBm. */
