/* book Worked example 2: Q: A resonant half-wave dipole (ZA = 73 Ω, D = 1.64) receives a 100 MHz wave of field strength 1 mV/m (peak), polarization matched. Find (a) Voc, (b) the power into a matched 73 Ω load, (c) the same power from S and Aem, and (d) the power into a 50 Ω receiver.
   1. λ = 3 m; leff = λ/π = 0.955 m.
   2. (a) Voc = E leff = 10⁻³ × 0.955 = 0.955 mV.
   3. (b) PL = Voc²/(8Rr) = (0.955 × 10⁻³)²/(8 × 73) = 1.56 × 10⁻⁹ W = 1.56 nW, that is −58.1 dBm.
   4. (c) S = E²/(2η) = 10⁻⁶/754 = 1.326 × 10⁻⁹ W/m²; Aem = 1.64 × 9/4π = 1.175 m² (1.177 with D = 1.641); P = S Aem = 1.56 × 10⁻⁹ W. The two routes agree.
   5. (d) With a 50 Ω load: I = Voc/(73 + 50) and P = ½ I² × 50 = (0.955 × 10⁻³)² × 50 / (2 × 123²) = 1.51 × 10⁻⁹ W.
   6. Ratio 1.51/1.56 = 0.965, which is 1 − |Γ|² with Γ = (50 − 73)/(50 + 73) = −0.187: a loss of only 0.15 dB.
   Answer: Voc = 0.955 mV; 1.56 nW (−58.1 dBm) matched, by both routes; 1.51 nW into 50 Ω, a 0.15 dB mismatch loss. */
