/* book: lead: The Friis transmission equation gives the power a receiving antenna collects from a transmitter at distance d in free space. It multiplies the transmit power by both antenna gains and divides by the spreading of the wave. Written in decibels it becomes a plain sum of gains and losses, the link budget, which is checked against the receiver’s sensitivity to find the margin. Wi-Fi, point-to-point mic */
