/* book exam traps: Dropping one of the two gains. Friis has both Gt and Gr. | Putting dB values into the ratio form, or ratios into the dB form. A 20 dBi antenna enters the product form as 100 and the dB form as 20. | Using d in km with λ in m in 20 log₁₀(4πd/λ). Only the 32.44 form takes MHz and km. | Treating FSPL as the only loss. Feeder, mismatch, polarization and pointing losses are added on top. | Getting the margin backwards. M = Pr − Psens; with Psens = −90 dBm and Pr = −62 dBm the margin is +28 dB. */
